{
  "id": "energy",
  "title": "Energy",
  "description": "Energy is the capacity to do work. This tool helps calculate energy efficiency and convert between energy units.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Energy\n\nEnergy is **the capacity (or capability) to do work.**\n\nEnergy is used or consumed when work is done.\n\nThe SI unit for energy is _joule - J_, where\n\n_1 J = 1 Nm_\n\n#### Imperial Units of Energy\n\n- _1 J = 0.738 ft lb_\n- _1 ft lb = 1.356 Nm (J)_\n\n### Energy Forms\n\nThere can be several forms of energy, including:\n\n- Mechanical energy\n- Heat or thermal energy\n- Electrical energy\n- Chemical energy\n- Nuclear energy\n- Light energy\n\n### Energy Efficiency\n\nEnergy efficiency is the ratio between useful energy output and input energy:\n\n_μ = Eo / Ei_\n\nwhere:\n- _μ = energy efficiency_\n- _Eo = useful energy output_\n- _Ei = energy input_"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Energy Efficiency Calculator"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "force",
          "label": "Force",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "N",
          "defaultValue": 100
        },
        {
          "id": "distance",
          "label": "Distance",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "inputEnergy",
          "label": "Input Energy",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "J",
          "defaultValue": 1500
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "outputEnergy",
          "label": "Useful Energy Output",
          "formula": "inputs.force * inputs.distance",
          "unit": "J"
        },
        {
          "id": "efficiency",
          "label": "Energy Efficiency",
          "formula": "inputs.force * inputs.distance / inputs.inputEnergy",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "efficiencyPercent",
          "label": "Energy Efficiency",
          "formula": "(inputs.force * inputs.distance / inputs.inputEnergy) * 100",
          "unit": "%",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Unit",
        "Conversion Factor",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Joule (J)",
          "1",
          "SI unit of energy"
        ],
        [
          "Newton-meter (Nm)",
          "1",
          "Equivalent to Joule"
        ],
        [
          "Foot-pound (ft lb)",
          "0.738",
          "1 J = 0.738 ft lb"
        ],
        [
          "Foot-pound (ft lb)",
          "1.356",
          "1 ft lb = 1.356 J"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}